WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.201
-Last time you were on our show,

00:00:02.201 --> 00:00:03.435
the world
was a different place.

00:00:03.435 --> 00:00:06.373
We went all over New York City,

00:00:06.373 --> 00:00:08.707
Grand Central Terminal,
Katz's Deli.

00:00:08.707 --> 00:00:10.409
We were on the subway.

00:00:10.409 --> 00:00:11.978
Do you have a favorite part
of that day?

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:14.246
-Grand Central.
-Yeah.

00:00:14.246 --> 00:00:16.816
-Subway.
-Subway.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.689 line:0%
-Yeah!

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:26.092 line:0%
-Korean heart!
-Yeah!

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:30.930
-I think my favorite
was in Grand Central when --

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.532
'Cause we had --
it was 3:00 in the morning.

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:33.733
There was no one there,
just you guys,

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:35.568
and I was standing back,
watching.

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:38.604
And the choreography
was so perfect.

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:40.306
And it sounded so great.

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:41.807
I mean, I've never seen
dancing like this.

00:00:41.807 --> 00:00:43.409
You were jumping
over each other,

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:45.277
people jumping in,
and doing that.

00:00:45.277 --> 00:00:47.646
I go, "Oh, my gosh."
And I remember I went up

00:00:47.646 --> 00:00:53.119
to Jungkook -- this was back
when you could hug somebody.

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.453
And I went over,
I gave you a hug,

00:00:54.453 --> 00:00:57.256
I go, "That was great, buddy,"
and I gave you a hug.

00:00:57.256 --> 00:00:58.724
And I could feel --

00:00:58.724 --> 00:01:01.761
I could feel your heart beating
through your back.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:03.196
[ Laughter ]
-Oh!

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:06.165
-It was like,
"These guys are working hard."

00:01:06.165 --> 00:01:08.968
It was so impressive.

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:10.270
And this was
3:00 in the morning,

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:11.770
4:00 in the morning in New York.

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:13.806
And I was like,
"These guys, man.

00:01:13.806 --> 00:01:15.441
That's why
they're the biggest band.

00:01:15.441 --> 00:01:16.843
They're putting the work in."

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:20.413
-Jimmy, actually,
we've never taken a train

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:23.283
or a subway in New York.
Never done it.

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:25.218
So we don't know --
we didn't know, like,

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:29.422
how important
or big the station was.

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:31.657
But you know, looking at you,
you were like --

00:01:31.657 --> 00:01:35.394
you was telling me, "Do you know
how important this is?

00:01:35.394 --> 00:01:37.096
Do you know how big this is?"

00:01:37.096 --> 00:01:41.667
And looking at you, that time we
got, like, "Yo, this is big!

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:44.070
Jimmy's so nervous!"
-[ Laughing ]

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.205
-That was
the most impressive moment.

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:47.440
-I was so nervous, so excited.
-Yeah.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.108
-You knocked it out of the park.
It was great.

00:01:49.108 --> 00:01:51.644
One of the things
your fans love about BTS

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:53.646
is how much you give back.

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:56.516
When COVID-19 broke out,
you made a bunch of donations

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:59.518
to help people
affected by the virus.

00:01:59.518 --> 00:02:03.690
You also donated
$1 million to concert crews,

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:06.459
the crew that
is out of work right now.

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:08.828
Is giving back something that
was always important to you?

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:13.199
-We just wanted to help
and do what we can

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:15.768
so that things can get better.

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:18.871
-You guys
gave a great graduation speech

00:02:18.871 --> 00:02:22.641
as part of YouTube's
"Dear class of 2020" event.

00:02:22.641 --> 00:02:24.977
Does it make you think about
your own high school experience?

00:02:24.977 --> 00:02:27.313
What were you guys like
back then?

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:29.381
RM, do you want to start?
What were you like?

00:02:29.381 --> 00:02:31.417
-I was like --
kind of like a nerd.

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:32.885
I was, like, all about studying.

00:02:32.885 --> 00:02:36.088
And I just liked to listen to
rap music like Eminem and Nas,

00:02:36.088 --> 00:02:39.192
but I was just, like, a --
just a good student.

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:40.493
-V, how about you?

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:04.750
-"V, wake up."
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:06.986
-Jimmy!
-Good boy, good boy.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:08.587
Jimin, that's awesome.
Respect, respect.

00:03:08.587 --> 00:03:13.026
-Jimin, good boy.
Me too, good boy.

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:14.594
-You bad boy.
-Bad boy.

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:16.629
-Jimin, what were you like
in high school?

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:55.801
-Jin, I didn't skip over you.

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:57.303
What were you like
in high school?

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:14.120
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:16.189
-You don't have to,
you don't have to have one.

00:04:16.189 --> 00:04:17.357
Suga?

00:04:44.483 --> 00:04:45.617
-Bad boy.
-Bad!

00:04:45.617 --> 00:04:49.822
-No, no.
-That's not good.

00:04:49.822 --> 00:04:51.023
-J-Hope.
-Bad boy.

00:04:51.023 --> 00:04:53.092
-J-Hope, I think that
you were like --

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:56.562
probably, like,
a big performer in high school.

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:58.798
Am I -- Am I right?
-That's right.

00:05:14.313 --> 00:05:15.881
-That's hilarious.
That's --

00:05:15.881 --> 00:05:18.350
I could see that,
I could see that.

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:22.188
Jungkook, when you were
in high school,

00:05:22.188 --> 00:05:25.491
the band was actually at your
high school graduation?

00:05:53.185 --> 00:05:55.754
What would you say to any kid
out there who's watching

00:05:55.754 --> 00:05:58.358
and dreams of being
the next BTS?

00:06:10.068 --> 00:06:12.071
-That's good advice.
That's great advice.

00:06:12.071 --> 00:06:14.407
-Yeah!
-Yeah, yeah!

00:06:14.407 --> 00:06:18.110
[ Applause ]

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:21.046
-Applause, applause!
-Oh, my gosh.

00:06:21.046 --> 00:06:24.049
What I really do love
about you guys,

00:06:24.049 --> 00:06:26.585
from working with you
and seeing you work is,

00:06:26.585 --> 00:06:28.420
you have great work ethic.

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:31.790
You really are professional,
but you're also very funny.

00:06:31.790 --> 00:06:34.260
You have a sense --
a great sense of humor.

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:36.162
And please don't ever lose that.

00:06:36.162 --> 00:06:39.131
-We gonna take your crown,
Jimmy!

00:06:39.131 --> 00:06:41.667
-[ Laughing ]

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:44.069
We have another incredible
performance from you guys

00:06:44.069 --> 00:06:45.538
later tonight in the show.

00:06:45.538 --> 00:06:48.640
BTS will be performing
"Black Swan."

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:51.009
BTS, everybody!

00:06:51.009 --> 00:06:54.780
Their new album, "BE,"
